`aghq` is an R package that uses quadrature to approximate the posterior using a TMB object. It has some similarities to INLA for using Laplace for inner marginalization but then using adaptive gauss hermite quadrature for the outer marginalization to get p(data).
awstringer1/aghq: Adaptive Gauss Hermite Quadrature for Bayesian Inference <https://github.com/awstringer1/aghq/>
[2102.06801] Stochastic Convergence Rates and Applications of Adaptive Quadrature in Bayesian Inference <https://arxiv.org/abs/2102.06801>

See the vignette for:  `normalized_posterior$lognormconst` from the built object to get the normalizing constant.... I think but double check.
[2101.04468] Implementing Approximate Bayesian Inference using Adaptive Quadrature: the aghq Package <https://arxiv.org/abs/2101.04468>

Related package in NIMBLE: Using nimbleQuad for maximum likelihood estimation and deterministic posterior approximation <https://r-nimble.org/vignettes/nimbleQuad.html>

